  "Z_tex": "Z = \\sum_{a\\in\\mathbb{Z}_5}\\Big(\\sum_{j=0}^{4}|\\chi_{(a;\\,j)}|^2 + |\\chi^{+}_{(a;\\,5)}|^2 + |\\chi^{-}_{(a;\\,5)}|^2\\Big)",
  "character_tex": "$b_{(a;\\,j)}$ are the branching functions of $SU(5)_1$ into the principal $SU(2)_{20}$: $\\chi^{SU(5)_1}_{a}(q, z^{2\\rho^\\vee}) = \\sum_{j} b_{(a;\\,j)}(q)\\, \\chi^{SU(2)_{20}}_{j}(q, z)$, $a\\in\\mathbb{Z}_5$ labelling $\\mathbf{1},\\mathbf{5},\\mathbf{10},\\overline{\\mathbf{10}},\\overline{\\mathbf{5}}$ and $j\\in\\{0,1,\\dots,10\\}$, with $b_{(a;\\,j)} = b_{(a;\\,10-j)}$. Blocks: $\\chi_{(a;\\,j)} = b_{(a;\\,j)}$ for $j\\le4$, and for the fixed points $\\chi^{\\pm}_{(a;\\,5)} = \\tfrac12\\big(b_{(a;\\,5)} \\pm \\delta_a\\big)$ with Lee–Yang characters $\\delta_{\\pm1} = q^{-1/60}G(q)$, $\\delta_{\\pm2} = q^{11/60}H(q)$ and $\\delta_0 = 0$, where $G = \\prod_{n\\ge0}[(1-q^{5n+1})(1-q^{5n+4})]^{-1}$ and $H = \\prod_{n\\ge0}[(1-q^{5n+2})(1-q^{5n+3})]^{-1}$ (Rogers–Ramanujan).",
  "description": "Weyl–Kac characters of $SU(5)_1$ specialised along the principal grading $e^{\\beta}\\to z^{\\langle\\beta,2\\rho^\\vee\\rangle}$ (checked against the $A_4$ lattice theta functions) are decomposed exactly into $SU(2)_{20}$ characters. The principal subgroup is $SO(3)$, so only integer $j$ occur and field identification is $(a;j)\\sim(a;10-j)$. Its fixed points $(a;5)$ are resolved (Schellekens–Yankielowicz 1990): the twining characters transform with $i$ times the $SU(5)_1$ $S$-matrix, are odd under $a\\to-a$, and are therefore Lee–Yang characters; the resulting 35 characters are non-negative integer series and transform correctly under the resolved $S$-matrix, which has non-negative integer fusion rules. Diagonal invariant.",
